	"joel_and_malachi_numbering_chirho": {
		"what_chirho": "Hebrew Bibles, and translations that follow them, count Joel in four chapters and Malachi in three: Joel 2:28-32 is their chapter 3, Joel 3 is their chapter 4, and Malachi 4 is the end of their chapter 3.",
		"how_judged_chirho": "From file names alone: a recording that lists a Joel 4 and a Malachi 3 and no Malachi 4 is taken to number them so, and only when it is also on the list approved by name in src/lib/catalogue-chirho/stations-chirho/sources-chirho/davar_numbering_chirho.ts. Nobody has listened, and the maker has not confirmed it. The crosswalk is from the SBL Handbook of Style, appendix E, and SIL eng.vrs; they support the crosswalk, not the reading of any one recording.",
		"what_was_done_chirho": "On those recordings Joel 3 is their fourth file. Their second and third files of Joel are each a part of chapter 2 and are held back, so Joel 2 is not offered. Malachi 3 plays their third file, which is wider than Malachi 3 elsewhere: it also holds what other stations call Malachi 4 (Hebrew Malachi 3:19-24). Malachi 4 is not offered separately on those stations.",
